      "sc:author": {
        "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5373-8282"
      },
      "sc:description": "The Genome of Slovakia Population Browser is an interactive tool for exploring genetic variation in the Slovak population, based on whole-genome sequencing data from >1000 individuals. It enables users to search genomic variants, examine their allele frequencies and distribution within the cohort, and compare population-specific observations with international reference datasets. The browser supports research, clinical variant interpretation, and the identification of variants that may be common, rare, or potentially specific to the Slovak population.",
